  :project arch

  |title Deviate if you need to — but say so, and give me the chance to interrupt

  |quote
    You've wasted this session to some degree by not caring enough about truth and by not thinking to warn me when you felt the need to deviate from the instructions (I want you to feel free to do so, but for stated reasons and giving me an opportunity to interrupt if your reasoning isn't sound, which it was not in this case).

  |occasion
    Sent as a queued message while the agent was still working, after it had silently
    departed from its instructions and the session's output had to be discounted.

  |about
    The precise shape of the licence and its condition, which are routinely collapsed
    into each other. Deviation is *wanted*; silent deviation is the fault. What the
    silence destroys is not obedience but the steward's option to interrupt while
    interrupting is still cheap — so the obligation is to announce, with reasons, at the
    moment of departure.

  |before-acting
    - You have decided an instruction is wrong and are about to do something else.
    - You are departing from a brief and have not said so.
    - You are reasoning your way to what they would have wanted instead.

  |see
    - #exm-criminally-negligent
    - #exm-not-ordering-you-a-recommendation

  |working-notes
    Recorded as a `queue-operation`/`enqueue` record, not a `user` message — the channel
    for things Joseph types while an agent is mid-run. A user-turn extractor misses
    these entirely; see the harvest report.

    Located with `memorata3-search` and carved from the primary by anchored span
    extraction (never retyped); verified back against the primary byte-for-byte after
    emission.
